00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.650
ROBERT SAXBY: Yeah, so let's
take a step back and think

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.942
about what a recommendation is.

00:02:38.942 --> 00:02:46.050
So during this prolonged
period of partial lockdowns

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.390
and things, I found
myself doing more DIY.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.510
And then I go online,
and I buy the next tool

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:53.710
or the thing I need.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:56.140
And often when you buy
a product or service,

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.750
there are some
recommendations there.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.330
For example, if you
buy a drill, then they

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.380
might suggest you
some drill bits that

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.730
will help you drill through
wood or metal or something

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:06.643
like that.

00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:09.060
But there's a whole bunch of
stuff they could suggest you.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.580
They could suggest an
extra battery or something.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.250
Now, obviously, some
folks compile these lists

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.800
manually using their
specialist knowledge

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.240
that they have about the area.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.300
But now imagine that you
don't have a catalog of tens

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.450
of products or hundreds.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.320
You have thousands
or tens of thousands.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.340
And rather than trying to
compile a recommendation

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.950
list for all these products,
all these tens of thousands

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.240
of products, why not let your
customer website behavior,

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.830
for example,
actually drive that?

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.598
So we have a
recommendation system.

00:03:41.598 --> 00:03:43.140
We're looking at
the feedback that we

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.148
get from customers, whether it's
either explicit or implicit.

00:03:46.148 --> 00:03:48.690
Implicit is the one we're going
after here because what we're

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.000
trying to do is infer
what customers like

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.400
by how often they
go back to a page

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.350
or how long they look at an
article, these kinds of things.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.350
And then when we
take that, we're

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.340
able to correlate what
the item that someone

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.020
was looking at with other
items that they look at next.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.180
And this we put into a system.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.160
And basically what
we draw out of that

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.680
is a list of
products or services

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.310
that our customers
are actively, based

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.490
on their current behavior,
interested in buying

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.589
when they look at this
product or service.

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:22.290
And then when we get a customer
and they look at a product,

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.950
we can then recommend them
one of these alternative

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.460
or complementary products.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.910
So it's real value there.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.530
It helps you to
upsell, cross-sell.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.990
It helps you to build a
better customer experience.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.620
And there are many
ways of actually

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.360
going about building this.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.190
The way that we've
got here is really

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:46.285
taking a canonical approach
based on the systems

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.910
that we make available
in Google Cloud.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.250
So BigQuery, if you're
a data warehouse.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.750
We're using Google
Analytics data,

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.230
which is a way to instrument
your website in order

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.320
to see what folks are doing, how
long they spend on page, which

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.530
page they go to next,
all that kind of stuff,

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.280
like the click-through
rates, convergence,

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.910
the things that are important
to analyze from your website.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.390
We have a service that brings
that data into BigQuery.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.140
And then in BigQuery,
as well, we actually

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.930
have an ML capability.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:17.400
So we're able to generate,
based on the Analytics data,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.950
recommendations using a model--

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.170
matrix factorization,
in this case--

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:26.330
and generate that list of
recommendations per product.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:27.800
And now, here's the great thing.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.140
It's not just-- as I
said, it's not just

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:34.710
about creating that list
or getting those insights.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.610
The next step is how
to activate that.

